{"id": "85846", "name": "משוואה ריבועית מבעיה מילולית – מידות מלבן לפי שטח, סעיפים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>A rectangle has length {{CT:0}}cm greater than its width. If it has an area of \\({{CT:1}}cm^2\\), find the dimensions of the rectangle.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">a</span></div><p>Write down an equation which relates the side lengths to the area of the rectangle.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:eq]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">b</span></div><p>Solve your equation. Enter your answer as a set of numbers.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:sol]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">c</span></div><p>Hence, find the length of the shorter side.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans3]] cm</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans3]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:short]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Call the width \\(x\\), write the area as a product of the side lengths, and solve the resulting quadratic equation; only the positive root is a length.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Setting up the equation (part a)</b><br>If \\(x\\)cm is the width then \\((x+{{CT:2}})\\) is the length. Now the area is \\({{CT:1}}cm^2\\) and so<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:3}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Solving the equation (part b)</b><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:4}}=0 \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:5}} \\]</p>So that \\(x={{CT:6}}\\) or \\(x={{CT:7}}\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The shorter side (part c)</b><br>Since lengths are positive quantities \\(x&gt;0\\) and we discard the negative root. Hence the length of the shorter side, in cm, is<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ x={{CT:7}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 1, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 1, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 1, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "eq", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "SubstEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "ta1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "eq-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "eq-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "SubstEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "ta2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_tru